    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for mcphost",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for mcphost fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-41178: go.opentelemetry.io/otel/baggage: no rejection of raw-length headers in baggage parsing allows for DoS\n  via oversized inputs (bsc#1276612).\n- CVE-2026-81092: github.com/mark3labs/mcp-go/server: requests accepted in HTTP transports without Host header checks\n  can lead to tool usage and resource exposure in target server (bsc#1278013).\n\nChanges for mcphost:\n\n- Update github.com/mark3labs/mcp-go/server to v0.56.0.\n- Update go.opentelemetry.io/otel to 1.44.0.\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-SL-Micro-6.2-1619",
        "title": "Patchnames"
